":"spreading"},{"surface":"துறைவனொடு","parts":[{"text":"துறைவன்","lemma":"tuṟaivaṉ","gloss":"lord of the shore"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"oṭu","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with the lord of the shore"},{"surface":"ஒருநாள்","parts":[{"text":"ஒரு","lemma":"oru","gloss":"one"},{"text":"நாள்","lemma":"nāḷ","gloss":"day"}],"gloss":"one day"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நக்கது","parts":[{"text":"நக்கது","lemma":"நக்கது","gloss":"that we laughed"}],"gloss":"that we laughed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஓர்","parts":[{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ōr","gloss":"one/a certain"}],"gloss":"a single"},{"surface":"பழியும்","parts":[{"text":"பழி","lemma":"paḻi","gloss":"blame"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even/also"}],"gloss":"even blame"},{"surface":"இலமே","parts":[{"text":"இலம்","lemma":"ilam","gloss":"we do not have"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"we do not have indeed"},{"surface":"போது","parts":[{"text":"போது","lemma":"pōtu","gloss":"flower bud"}],"gloss":"buds"},{"surface":"அவிழ்","parts":[{"text":"அவிழ்","lemma":"aviḻ","gloss":"open/unfold"}],"gloss":"opening"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பொன்","parts":[{"text":"பொன்","lemma":"poṉ","gloss":"gold"}],"gloss":"golden"},{"surface":"இணர்","parts":[{"text":"இணர்","lemma":"iṇar","gloss":"flower cluster"}],"gloss":"clusters"},{"surface":"மரீஇய","parts":[{"text":"மரீஇய","lemma":"மரீஇய","gloss":"associated/filled with"}],"gloss":"associated/filled with","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"புள்","parts":[{"text":"புள்","lemma":"puḷ","gloss":"bird"}],"gloss":"birds"},{"surface":"இமிழ்","parts":[{"text":"இமிழ்","lemma":"imiḻ","gloss":"chirp/sound"}],"gloss":"chirping"},{"surface":"பொங்கர்","parts":[{"text":"பொங்கர்","lemma":"poṅkar","gloss":"branch/grove"}],"gloss":"branches"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புன்னை","parts":[{"text":"புன்னை","lemma":"puṉṉai","gloss":"mastwood tree (Punnai)"}],"gloss":"Punnai tree"},{"surface":"அம்","parts":[{"text":"அம்","lemma":"am","gloss":"beautiful"}],"gloss":"beautiful"},{"surface":"சேரி","parts":[{"text":"சேரி","lemma":"cēri","gloss":"street/neighborhood"}],"gloss":"street"},{"surface":"இவ்வூர்","parts":[{"text":"இவ்வூர்","lemma":"இவ்வூர்","gloss":"this town"}],"gloss":"this town","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கொன்னலர்","parts":[{"text":"கொன்னலர்","lemma":"கொன்னலர்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தூற்றந்தன்","parts":[{"text":"தூற்றந்தன்","lemma":"தூற்றந்தன்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கொடுமை","parts":[{"text":"கொடுமை","lemma":"கொடுமை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"யானே","parts":[{"text":"யானே","lemma":"யானே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"Great ocean fishermen's caught fish drying / rare backwater caught prawn's dried meat with / moonlight-colored white sand smelling of fish, in many ways together / on every sand dune spreading, the lord of the shore with, one day / laughed, that kind of blame even we do not have! Buds opening / golden clusters associated, birds chirping branches of / Punnai-tree-beautiful street of this town / uselessly rumors spreads, by its own cruelty!","translation":"We do not have even a speck of blame from having laughed with the lord of the shore on a single day—he whose shore is where the fishermen of the great ocean dry their catch, and along with the dried prawns caught in the rare backwaters, the fishy smell spreads over all the sand dunes of moonlight-white sand. Yet, this town, with its beautiful streets of Punnai trees whose branches are filled with golden clusters of opening buds and chirping birds, uselessly spreads rumors out of its own sheer cruelty!","modern":"பெரிய கடல் மீனவர்கள் பிடித்த மீன்களைக் காயவைக்கும் உலர்மீன் வாசனை, அரிய கழிகளில் பிடித்த இறால் மீனின் உலர்மீன் வாசனையோடு சேர்ந்து, நிலவின் நிறத்தைக் கொண்ட வெண்மையான மணல் பரப்பில் வீச, மணல் மேடுகள் எங்கும் பரவுகின்ற கடற்கரைத் தலைவனுடன் ஒருநாள் நாம் கூடி மகிழ்ந்தோம். அதனால் நமக்கு எந்தப் பழியும் இல்லை. ஆனால், மலரும் அரும்புகளையும் பொன்னிறப் பூங்கொத்துகளையும் கொண்ட, பறவைகள் ஒலிக்கும் கிளைகளையுடைய புன்னை மரங்கள் நிறைந்த அழகிய தெருக்களைக் கொண்ட இவ்வூர், தன் கொடுமையினாலேயே வீணான அலர் தூற்றுகின்றது.","explanation":"The heroine is speaking to her friend (tōḻi) within the hearing of the hero who is waiting nearby to arrange their marriage. She describes the hero's maritime landscape (neytal), where the smell of drying ocean fish and backwater prawns spreads over the moonlight-white sand dunes. She points out that they only spent a single day laughing and talking together, which brought no actual blame or wrongdoing. Yet, the townspeople in their beautiful neighborhood of blooming Punnai trees and chirping birds are cruelly spreading groundless rumors (alar) about them. This description of the landscape, where the fishy smell overpowers the white sand, subtly implies how the town's ugly rumors are overshadowing the pure and innocent love of the couple, urging the hero to marry her soon.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}